—It felt as if a distant steam whistle had sounded, and his consciousness slowly surfaced.

Breaking through the water's surface of wakefulness, the first thing he felt upon emerging was a stinging, burning pain. Sensing it intensely stimulating his entire body, especially his right arm, an anguished groan involuntarily rattled in his throat.

"—Gh."

"—! Subaru, have you woken up, I wonder? Are you alright, I suppose?"

Hearing his escaped moan, a voice quickly noticed his awakening. It was a familiar one—his partner Beatrice, with whom he greeted every morning's wakefulness. However, waking up accompanied by pain like this was vastly different from those daily occurrences.

"Bea...ko...? What... happened to me...?"

"You mustn't force yourself to sit up, I wonder. Your burns are still severe, I suppose. ...If only I had enough mana, Betty would heal you right away. I'm sorry, I suppose."

"That's not something you need to apologize for... Burns?"

Timidly opening his eyelids, he saw Beatrice's downcast face peering at him. The Great Spirit, her large, round eyes filled with sorrow—he instinctively moved to comfort her lament, and then stopped.

Hearing the word 'burns,' his sleeping brain began to awaken, lagging behind his body. Right. He was sure he had seen flames just before losing consciousness. And just before that—

"—Crusch-san!"

Remembering the tragedy at the MacMahon manor, Subaru forcefully sat up.

Once he started remembering, the vivid memories rapidly began restoring themselves all at once. Miklotov's death, Crusch confessing that she had done it with her own hands, the scene of trying to apprehend her, and the "Dragon's Eye" residing in the resisting Crusch's left eye—things had simply moved with too much furious momentum.

But the first priority was Crusch. At the very end, using E・M・M and Invisible Providence, Subaru had succeeded in restraining her. After that, the sudden flames had appeared—

"Right, there was an insane burst of fire... The pain in my arm, is that from the burns? Damn, it stings...! But, something like this is nothing—"

"W-Wait, calm down, I suppose! I can't cast healing magic on you because I'm short on mana, I wonder! If you don't stay quiet and rest, you might catch some terrible illness, I suppose!"

"This is no time for that! Right now, Crusch-san comes before me. Me running a fever and collapsing, compared to that, doesn't matter—"

It was just as he was about to declare that and shake off Beatrice's worry.

"—It seems you've awoken, Natsuki Subaru."

"Eh."

Suddenly, an unexpected voice was heard, and Subaru's eyes widened. Emerging from the darkness at the edge of his vision was none other than Crusch, whom he had been just about to go search for.

Her left eye covered again with an eyepatch, she illuminated the surroundings with a handheld Lagmite ore lamp. Crusch approached Subaru, who was locked in a back-and-forth with Beatrice. Taking hold of his right arm, she said:

"As I thought, this is not a wound to be left untreated. Only first aid, but take this."

As she spoke, Crusch set the lamp at her feet. She then took an embroidered white handkerchief from her breast pocket and gently wrapped it around Subaru's right arm in place of a bandage.

At the sight of the handkerchief, touching the throbbing burn wound, becoming stained, and the gentleness of Crusch's hands as she wrapped it, Subaru—completely unable to keep up with the situation—just blinked in bewilderment.

"—? What is the matter? A wind of confusion is blowing over you."

"...Well, yeah, it's blowing at gale force. According to my memory, until just a moment ago, we were, like, going at each other with desperate looks on our faces, right?"

"I believe the only one with a desperate look on his face was you, Sir."

"I'm talking about the overall picture! If the two of us were doing it and I had a desperate look, that means fifty percent of the situation was desperate, doesn't it?"

"I see. That does sound reasonable."

Seeing her nod with a dead-serious face, Subaru could only stare dumbfounded at having his flippant remark answered with another.

Only then did Subaru finally realize that they were in a strange location—exchanging words in a damp, hardly sanitary passageway. He had been laid on a cold, hard floor. The air was clammy with a fishy smell. Realizing it afresh, it was a space filled with an undeniable sewage-like sensation, difficult to ignore.

"Or rather, is this literally just a sewer?"

"That's one reason why I don't want you pushing yourself, I suppose. If you carelessly get tetanus or something, even treating it would be a struggle right now, I suppose."

"So you're pulling double duty as pretty doctor and tomboy nurse... I'm incredibly grateful for that, but more importantly—what the hell is going on?"

"—"

Showing understanding for Beatrice's concern for his well-being, what Subaru still couldn't grasp was the fact that Crusch—just as dedicated as his devoted partner—was actively tending to his burns.

Narrowing her eyes slightly at Subaru's lowered voice, Crusch let out a quiet breath and said:

"This is a sewer some distance from the MacMahon estate. By travel distance, it's roughly between the Noble District and the Commercial District. Even using the sewers, the checkpoints managing passage to the upper levels cannot be bypassed. Currently, that is our obstacle."

"Wait, wait, please wait. I'm not following the conversation at all. For starters, the stuff right around when I blacked out is super hazy. But—"

"But?"

"From what you're saying now... could it be that right now, me and Crusch-san are in the same party?"

"Party..."

Crusch frowned at the unfamiliar term. However, to Subaru's question, Beatrice—who had properly passed the second level of the Modern Language Proficiency Test—nodded, "I suppose."

"Various troublesome things are tangled up, but that girl bears no hostility toward Betty and the others, I suppose. It was also that girl who carried the unconscious Subaru all the way here, I suppose."

"If you had been left in that place, you would likewise have been unable to avoid death by burning. At the very least, I sensed no falsehood in your words. If so, your death is not something I desire."

"Is that so. That's, thank you... but..."

The last scene before he lost consciousness, and the trace of the large burn on his right arm, half-proved the truth that he had been saved from a dangerous situation by Crusch. There was no way Beatrice would collude with Crusch just to deceive Subaru.

However, the reason Subaru couldn't honestly express his thanks was Crusch's phrasing—Subaru's death was not something she desired. But what about the deaths of Miklotov and the others?

"...Crusch-san, did you really cut down Miklotov-san?"

"—. I affirmed it there as well, but it is a fact. Miklotov MacMahon and the estate staff he employed—each and every one was cut down by my hand."

"—!"

"Is an explanation of the reason also necessary? This too is a repetition of what was discussed there, but Miklotov MacMahon and his associates were usurpers, existences that posed a threat to the Kingdom of Lugunica. Therefore, as a senior noble, I meted out punishment by the sword."

"That... that's what I don't get. Usurpers, threats to the Kingdom—what does any of that mean? Was he plotting something so stupid that Crusch-san couldn't stand it?"

"—At the very least, there is a high possibility that he was exploiting the Dragon History Stone for convenience."

Subaru gasped, trying to burst the bubbles of doubt welling up one after another in order to advance the conversation.

The information Crusch added last was precisely related to the 'Dragon History Stone'—something Subaru had wanted to confirm directly with Miklotov today.

In the Kingdom, the covenant with the "Divine Dragon," which held enormously strong influence, and the prophetic tablet engraved with matters concerning it—that was the 'Dragon History Stone.' It was also the key item that became the basis for initiating the Royal Selection, in which Emilia was participating.

However, as it was an object he had only heard about and never seen in person, Subaru had thought that, if possible, he wanted to confirm its existence with his own eyes directly.

"That Dragon History Stone was being exploited? By Miklotov-san?"

"It is difficult to imagine that the Dragon History Stone, which is meant to convey grave national matters, did not speak of the successive deaths of the Royal Family. If that is the case, what is plausible is that someone in a position entrusted with the Dragon History Stone intentionally concealed a prophecy that should have been made and withheld it from the public."

"But... but, isn't that a bit too late to be bringing up!? In the first place, that doubt should have existed before the Royal Selection even started. Especially for you, Crusch-san, and Ferris—"

There should have been motivation to investigate the details of the anomaly in which the Royal Family perished. After all, they had a particularly close relationship with the Fourth Prince, one of the deceased royals.

Though, Subaru wasn't tactless enough to voice that and press the point.

"—That I failed to entertain the possibility of doubt is a matter of my deepest regret."

Extrapolating the end of the words Subaru left unspoken, Crusch acknowledged her own mistake.

Of course, calling it a mistake showed a cruel lack of compassion toward someone who had just recently lost a person close to them. Subaru had also heard from Ferris that the relationship between Crusch and the Fourth Prince was more than just simply a close one. So much so that it was likely the greatest motivation behind Crusch desiring the throne.

But—

"Then, why would you suddenly start suspecting it now...?"

"Should I not need to say it? They sent the 'Divine Dragon Church' to my side, deceived Ferris with cunning words, and schemed to force me to withdraw from the Royal Selection."

"—!? Crusch-san, that's—"

"Ferris has a strong sense of responsibility. My circumstances were what they were, and the mental strain had taken its toll. On top of that, having sweet whispers poured into his ear by someone known as the brain of the Kingdom, it is no surprise Ferris made an error in judgment. Unless that were the case—"

"——"

"—Unless that were the case, there is no way he would ever do something that tramples on the vow between myself and His Highness."

Crusch lowered her eyes, dropped her voice, and struggled to suppress her emotions. But the more her effort was conveyed, the more Subaru lost sight of which direction to tip the scales within his heart.

Emotionally, of course, he wanted to believe in Crusch. He felt bad for Miklotov, but if he had truly been a usurper exploiting the Kingdom for personal gain, then Crusch's actions would carry legitimacy. Perhaps, in a proper trial, there could be room for consideration of extenuating circumstances.

But Subaru remembered Miklotov's words—how, even after Subaru had exposed such a shameful, unpresentable display at the Royal Selection hall, he had still acknowledged him as Emilia's knight.

Crusch was Subaru's benefactor. And Miklotov was likewise a benefactor. Wishing for a conveniently one-sided conclusion felt impossibly difficult.

And besides—

"Ferris..."

Ferris, resolved to be hated by Crusch and even dismissed from his knighthood, had taken the hand extended by the "Divine Dragon Church" and made a choice with the possibility of his lord's withdrawal from the Royal Selection in view.

Even if that meant rendering void the vow surrounding the Fourth Prince, he had chosen it.

Subaru did not want to simply dismiss that decision as the result of being deceived by someone.

"...I get what you're saying, Crusch-san. For now, anyway. I want to talk this through thoroughly. There are a few other things as well—"

"Wait, Natsuki Subaru. Your questions are entirely reasonable, but if you have awakened, I wish to prioritize moving. It is unwise to remain in this place indefinitely."

"Ah—the location, you mean the sewer? I do want to move somewhere else, sure, but we still haven't finished talking..."

As Crusch slowly shook her head, trying to wind down the conversation, Subaru persisted. However, Beatrice pulled on the sleeve of Subaru's unburned left arm. Glancing at her, he saw a slight tension dwelling in her expression.

"On this matter, Betty agrees with that girl, I suppose. Anyway, let's escape first, I wonder. If we dawdle, we'll be caught by pursuers, I suppose."

"Even you're saying that... wait, wait, I can't let that slide. Escape? Pursuers? I don't get it. So the fact that we're in a sewer is basically..."

"——"

"...basically, like we're... on the run..."

As he put it into words, a gradually gathering ominous premonition numbed Subaru's tongue. Meanwhile, Crusch once again lifted the lamp she had placed in the passage. Beatrice, wearing a troubled frown, repeatedly opened and closed her thin lips slightly, as if wondering how best to say it.

He could infer from their no-nonsense attitudes and consideration-filled demeanors. —That, no joke, Subaru and the others had been driven into the position of fugitives.

"I don't get it! There's way too much missing explanation! And besides..."

Speaking, Subaru looked around, confirmed that there was no one else besides Beatrice and Crusch, and pointed out the glaring unnaturalness. —Tiga's absence.

"Where's Tiga...? That guy was in the mansion with us too. So what's the deal with him not being here? What's what, why, how, and how did it come to this? I want to hear that story—"

"—Tiga Rauleon, was it? Unfortunately, that man is our pursuer."

"...What?"

Crusch's voice, responding to his question, however, gave birth to a new question in Subaru.

Something he couldn't understand, stacked atop something else he couldn't understand—it was only natural that the overall shape of this tower of incomprehensible building blocks became impossible to grasp. Feeling precisely that way, blinking in bewilderment, Subaru looked at Crusch.

Then, meeting Subaru's questioning gaze, she raised the lamp, illuminating her beautiful features—left eye covered by an eyepatch—with its white light, and continued.

It was—

"Currently, you and I are being pursued. By Tiga Rauleon, and by the Royal Army. —On suspicion of the murder of Miklotov MacMahon and of being usurpers scheming to overthrow the Kingdom."
